        "width": "full-width",
        "title": "",
        "text": "<h2>What You'll Find in the Garage Sale</h2><p>Not every discount here exists for the same reason, and it helps to know what you are looking at.</p><p>Some items are overstock, which means we simply ordered more than we needed and are moving the surplus at a lower price. Others are closeouts or discontinued models that we are clearing to make room for newer versions, like products being phased out in favor of an updated series. A few are new-old stock, meaning they are brand new units from earlier production runs. And many garage sale products are special-order items, which ship on a longer timeline than our regular in-stock catalog.</p><p>The condition and availability of each item are noted on its product page, so check the individual listing for the specifics before you buy. When a product is limited to the quantity on hand or will not be restocked, we say so directly on the page.</p><h2>Why These Prices Are Lower</h2><p>The markdown on a garage sale item reflects why we are clearing it, not a drop in quality. A discontinued lighthead still puts out the same light it did at full price. Overstock is priced to move because we have too much of it, not because anything is wrong with it. If an item has any condition notes worth knowing, you will find them on the product page. What you will not find is a hidden catch behind the discount.</p>",
        "heading_size": "medium",
        "text_alignment": "left"
      }
    },
    "dynamic_rich_text_kp7fCG": {
      "type": "dynamic-rich-text",
      "name": "t:sections.rich_text.presets.rich_text.name",
      "settings": {
        "width": "full-width",
        "title": "",
        "text": "<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><h3>What is the Strobes N' More Garage Sale? </h3><p>The Garage Sale is our clearance section for overstock, closeout, discontinued, and special-order emergency lighting. Everything here is offered at a reduced price, and the selection rotates as stock moves, so it is worth checking back.</p><h3>Are garage sale items new?</h3><p>Most garage sale items are new. Some are new-old stock from earlier production runs, and some are discontinued models we are clearing out. The condition of each item is described on its product page.</p><h3>Why are these products discounted?<strong> </strong></h3><p>Prices are reduced because the items are overstock, closeouts, discontinued models, or special-order clearance. The savings come from our need to move the inventory, not from any drop in product quality.</p><h3>Do garage sale items come with a warranty?</h3><p>Warranty coverage varies by product. Check the individual listing for warranty details, or call our team at (401) 454-4487 and we will confirm the coverage on a specific garage sale item before you buy.</p><h3>Can I return a garage sale item? </h3><p>Return eligibility can differ for clearance and special-order products. Review the details on the product page or reach out to us at (401) 454-4487 so we can walk you through the options on the item you are considering.</p><h3>How long does shipping take on garage sale items?<strong> </strong></h3><p>Many garage sale products are special-order items, so lead times can run longer than our regular in-stock catalog. If you need an item by a certain date, contact us for an estimated ship time before you order.</p><p></p><p>Browse the full garage sale selection above. Stock is limited and moves quickly, so if you see the light, beacon, or console you have been looking for, do not wait on it. Questions about a specific item? Call us at <a href=\"tel:4014544487\" title=\"tel:4014544487\">(401) 454-4487</a>, Monday through Friday, 8:30 am to 4:30 pm EST.</p>",
        "heading_size": "medium",
        "text_alignment": "left"
      }
    },
